atively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. So reliability high, stress resilience high, technical competence (weather, computer). But nasty remarks affect crew cooperation, professional communication. Weak memory for numbers could affect attention/accuracy.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Weakness: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence good, but communication and adaptability poor.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weakness: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. So reliability, attention, problem solving, responsibility good, but hot temper and know-it-all affect crew cooperation and professional communication.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some negatives. Which candidate has most strengths and least critical weaknesses? For long-distance pilot, crew cooperation and calm under pressure are crucial. Also responsibility, technical competence.\n\nCandidate B: strong stress handling, conscientious, good weather assessment, but nasty remarks could be serious for crew. That may be a red flag.\n\nCandidate C: calm, quick decisions, technical, but egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education (adaptability). Could be problematic.\n\nCandidate D: good problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all could affect crew. Hot temper is serious under pressure.\n\nCandidate A: anticipation, leadership, spatial vision, but show-off, not open to new ideas. Show-off may affect crew, but maybe less severe than hot temper? Not open to new ideas could affect adaptability.\n\nWe need to weigh. Which candidate has the least severe negative? Show-off vs nasty remarks vs egocentric vs hot temper. Nasty remarks likely severe. Hot temper also severe. Egocentric and communication difficulty also severe. Show-off maybe less severe? Not open to new ideas also concerning but maybe manageable.\n\nThus Candidate A might be best overall despite some negatives. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate A.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the initial overview...\" Provide evidence: anticipation dangerous situations, leadership, spatial vision; negatives: show-off, not open to new ideas. Argue that strengths outweigh negatives and others have more severe crew cooperation issues.\n\nThus vote Candidate A.\n\nNow produce output."}
